  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length concert at the Aladdin Theater in Portland, Oregon, on Tuesday, September 10, 2019 [1]. This event is the 291st show in the Internet Archive’s collection for the band, following a previous performance at the Crystal Ballroom on September 9, 2019 [2]. The recording, titled tmg2019-09-10, was taped and transferred by Liz Hamilton and contains 26 songs with a total runtime of 119 minutes [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific date [1]. The setlist opens with “Heretic Pride” and “You or Your Memory,” both from the album *The Sunset Tree* [1]. The band then plays “Moon Over Goldsboro” from *Get Lonely* and “Magpie” from *The Sunset Tree* [1]. Notable tracks include “Running Away with What Freud Said” from *Taboo VI: The Homecoming* and “Attention All Pickpockets” from the *Letter from Belgium* EP [1]. The performance features a partial rendition of Heart’s “Barracuda,” noted as unreleased [1]. Later in the set, songs from *In League with Dragons* such as “An Antidote for Strychnine” and “Younger” are played [1]. The main set concludes with “Cry for Judas” [1]. The encore sequence is extensive, featuring “Waylon Jennings Live!,” “Palmcorder Yajna,” and “The Diaz Brothers” [1]. Additional encore tracks include “Possum By Night,” “No Children,” “Up the Wolves,” “Going Invisible 2,” and “Liza Forever Minnelli” [1]. This recording offers a complete view of the band’s repertoire for this specific Portland show [1].",
